// The ASSIGNMENT axis of the C string-literal idiom, distinct from the decl-init axis in
// err_fixed_array_from_string_literal.cb. This spelling survived the decl-init fix: it
// compiled and printed garbage, and the indexed-read form killed the compiler. The exact
// failure text is build-dependent and was NOT reproducible on ca5a02a Release (see the
// 2026-08-02 correction in internal/issue/p1/llvm-cannot-select-sign-extend-on-const-array-index.md);
// what reproduces there is a bare SIGSEGV at exit 139 with no output.
expect_error("CFlat has no C-style character-array assignment") {
    void f() { char[8] b = default; b = "hello"; }
}
